        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to form three complete pairs in your hand.',
          gameplay: "1. Players draw a tile from the reserve and discard one into the center.\n2. A player can 'chow' (claim) an opponent's discard ONLY if it completes a pair.\n3. Pairs are laid face-down until the hand is won.",
          keyRules: [
            "Each turn: either claim the previous player's discard to complete a pair, or draw one from the reserve.",
            'After acquiring a tile, lay down any completed pairs face down, then discard one tile face up.',
            'First to complete three pairs wins. With 2 or 3 players, 6-6 cannot be the third pair; with 4 players it can.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize Civil pairs early as they are easier to recognize. Keep the Supreme pair (tiles 1-2 and 2-4) if you find them—they are rare and valuable.',
          intermediate: 'Efficiency: If you have a Military tile like 6-1, keep an eye out for its counterparts 5-2 or 4-3. Knowing the pip totals is essential for speed.',
          advanced: 'Discard Management: Watch what tiles others are discarding. If both 1-1 tiles have been discarded, any remaining single 1-1 is a dead tile and should be discarded immediately.',
          tips: [
            'Memorize the Military pairs (7s, 8s, 9s) to quickly identify matches.',
            'The Supreme pair (4-2 and 2-1) is the only pair that is neither identical nor shares a total.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
